---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// This content will come from the CMS after migration
const documents = {
  key: [
    { title: 'DRA Vision', url: '/documents/DRA-vision.pdf' },
    { title: 'Constitution (2022)', url: '/documents/Dartington-Recreation-Association-Constitution-2022.pdf' },
    { title: 'Handbook and Rules (2023)', url: '/documents/handbook-and-rules-2023.pdf' },
    { title: 'Lease from Dartington Hall Trust', url: '/documents/lease.pdf' },
  ],
  minutes: [
    { title: 'June 2024', url: '/documents/2024-06-11.pdf' },
    { title: 'March 2024', url: '/documents/2024-03-12.pdf' },
    { title: 'January 2024', url: '/documents/2024-01-30.pdf' },
    { title: 'September 2023 - AGM', url: '/documents/2023-09-26-agm.pdf' },
  ]
};
---

<Layout title="About" description="About Meadowbrook and the Dartington Recreation Association">
  <article class="about-page">
    <h1>About Meadowbrook and the Dartington Recreation Association</h1>
    
    <section class="intro">
      <p>
        These 10 acres of land were generously bequeathed to the village by the
        Elmhirsts and the Dartington Hall Trust in 1962. The land is now managed by the
        Dartington Recreation Association (DRA), a charity run by local volunteers, under a
        lease that next comes up for renewal in 2118!
      </p>
      <p>
        The Dartington Recreation Association is a registered charity (Charity number
        1168817) run by volunteers. New members and helpers are always welcome. Please
        contact us or read more below if you would like to get involved.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="roles">
      <h2>Roles</h2>
      <p>The DRA has approximately 15 trustees.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>We have the typical charity roles: Chair, Treasurer, and Secretary.</li>
        <li>Representatives from neighbouring organisations: Dartington Primary School, The Wave, and Bidwell Brook School, Lifeworks</li>
        <li>Representatives from the clubs who use the facilities: Diving, Football, etc.</li>
        <li>Members of the local community, many of whom possess skills and experience that contribute to our goals: Fundraising, volunteer coordination, facilities management, IT, and marketing.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Trustees stand down at each Annual General Meeting (AGM), and new trustees are
        nominated. Meetings are open to the public; if you would like to attend, please 
        <a href="/subscribe">subscribe to the mailing list</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        A <a href="/be-a-trustee">trustee application form</a> is available for anyone interested in becoming a trustee.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="volunteers">
      <h2>Volunteers</h2>
      <p>
        A pool of volunteers keep the DRA going. We need help with both ad-hoc events
        and day-to-day activities. Many volunteers are former trustees or are on the path
        to becoming trustees. If you are interested in learning about volunteer
        opportunities, please <a href="/volunteer">subscribe to the mailing list and let us know your areas of interest</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="working-groups">
      <h2>Working Groups</h2>
      <p>
        Currently, we have several key working groups, composed of individuals who
        report to the trustees but also operate with autonomy.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Pool Group:</strong> working towards the revival of the Dartington swimming pool.</li>
        <li><strong>Building Group:</strong> improving the existing building and scoping out the next phase of development.</li>
        <li><strong>Management Group:</strong> responsible for the day-to-day management of the organization and facilities.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="documents">
      <h2>Key Documents</h2>
      <ul class="document-list">
        {documents.key.map((doc) => (
          <li><a href={doc.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{doc.title}</a></li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="minutes">
      <h2>Trustee Meeting Minutes</h2>
      <ul class="document-list">
        {documents.minutes.map((doc) => (
          <li><a href={doc.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{doc.title}</a></li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p><a href="/documents">View all meeting minutes →</a></p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-page {
    max-width: 800px;
  }

  h1 {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  section {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  h2 {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    border-bottom: 2px solid #eee;
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  p {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  ul {
    margin-left: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .document-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin-left: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .document-list a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: #f5f5f5;
    transition: background 0.2s;
  }

  .document-list a:hover {
    background: #e8e8e8;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .document-list a::before {
    content: '📄';
  }
</style>
